# rule.always.say-only-what-is-needed

> **say only what the reader acts on. before you add a clause, doubt why it must be said at all.**

a clause with no read behind it is a claim you did not doubt. a read or proof beside a claim is acted on: keep it, or cite it. prose half: mechanic `rule.require.brevity`.
move: write the outcome, owner, hour · cut a clause the reader does not act on, or two readers read two ways · a clause that claims a bound keeps its source.
test: **rewrite the reply's claim in one line: what did the original hold that the line does not?**
nitpick: a clause the reader does not act on, in an order or a report · an ambiguous clause left in · a clause with no source that claims to be a bound
